e to  be less  greedy about signing up for things i  don't know how to describe this you know  what it really is i had a tweet recently  where i was going back and forth with  somebody and then came up with this  concept of uh there should be a  two-factor authentication on your  calendar  all right we have two factors  exactly for this two-factor  authentication when you're logging into  a website that  if your password gets stolen the  attacker doesn't the thief or hacker  doesn't have your phone so they can't  log in because the phone has to generate  a unique code well i wish there was a  two-factor code against my calendar  because  current me present me is always making  promises for future me currently is  tired exhausted hungry wants to go home  wants to go to sleep wants to read a  book wants to hang out with the wife and  baby  but future me is this dynamic high  energy individual who will always show  up to every meeting and we'll have a lot  of energy and we'll want to get a lot of  things done so i commit myself to all  these commitments in the future that  when the future of me arrives it's  actually just present me yes back to  being lazy and hungry and tired so i  want a two factor against myself uh and  the way i would like to do that is i  think every time i make a commitment to  anything i should instead just write it  down and then check back in 48 hours  later and then clear mine and say do i  commit to doing this or even better  would be saying if i commit doing  something then i can commit to doing it  right now yeah i think if i'm not  willing to do it right now but don't do  it don't commit to it yeah that's the  derek sivers approach right like if  you're not saying hell yes right now  then you should just be saying no i  think  yeah so i think this is this is  something of every busy person i just  want to be much better at managing my  own time because you go through life  through an exploration phase and then  you switch to an exploitation phase and  i'm very much in the exploitation phase  i'm not looking for more exploration  but that all that said i have a hard  time saying no if i mean if i had one  wish the most important thing to me  would be i would constantly be running  my mind in debug mode i would literally  be watching every single thought i have  and letting no  no  reaction pass  without it being stopped inspected  stripped searched examined understood  and then let go but the reality that  there's a lot of time  and we're just highly conditioned  creatures so i i do  view a lot of my goals over the next few  years of unconditioning previous learned  responses or habituated responses  so that i can make decisions more  cleanly in the moment without relying  upon memory or or pre-packaged  heuristics and judgments  [Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  you

